<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pakubuwono II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1711">1711</a>–<a href="/years/1749">1749</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Pakubuwana II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pakubuwana II was ruler of Mataram from 1726 to 1749. During the Chinese War of 1740–1743 he first sided with the rebels against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> and then changed sides; rebels sacked his capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kartasura">Kartasura</a> in 1742, and he regained it only with Company help and the cession of the north coast. He moved the court to Surakarta in 1745–1746.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pakubuwono-ii.jpg" alt="Pakubuwono II" width="320" height="389" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pakubuwana_II.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
